<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First War of Scottish Independence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1296–1328</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First War of Scottish Independence was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from Edward I's invasion in 1296 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-edinburgh-northampton">Treaty of Edinburgh–Northampton</a> in 1328. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-wallace">William Wallace</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-the-bruce">Robert the Bruce</a>, who won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stirling">Stirling</a> Bridge (1297) and Bannockburn (1314), the Scots resisted English conquest, and England finally recognised Scottish independence under Bruce.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence.jpg" alt="First War of Scottish Independence" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthew White Ridley · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_Stirling_Bridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
